[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105083,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ganglioneuroma is a benign sympathetic nervous system tumour composed mainly of Schwann cells, with a lesser component of ganglion cells, representing the differentiated mature tumour in the peripheral neuroblastic tumour continuum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105084,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9490/0 Ganglioneuroma</p>\r\n<p>9490/0 Maturing ganglioneuroma</p>\r\n<p>9490/0 Mature ganglioneuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105085,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A00.21 &amp; XH03L9 Mixed neuronal-glial tumours &amp; Ganglioneuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105086,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105087,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Maturing ganglioneuroma; mature ganglioneuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105088,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unlike neuroblastoma, ganglioneuroma occurs more commonly in the thorax than in the adrenal gland {11346873; 27465021; 29369484}. Tumours at unusual sites may represent matured metastases of a previous neuroblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105089,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority of ganglioneuromas are incidentally discovered during imaging for unrelated reasons {25501841}. Most are non-functioning {11346873; 27465021}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105090,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The exact incidence rate of this rare tumour is unknown. It mainly affects older children and young adults (median age: 6&nbsp;years) {18375900; 19530234; 29369484}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105091,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105092,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The Schwann cell origin is controversial. It is postulated that Schwann cells are recruited into the tumour by biologically favourable neuroblasts that produce factors critical for their proliferation and development {10421272; 15743800; 9788610}. In turn, Schwann cells can secrete antiproliferative and differentiation factors crucial for neuronal maturation. This process is very unlikely to occur in tumours with unfavourable histology that cannot differentiate {8618605}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105093,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ganglioneuroma is a firm, solid, unencapsulated white mass, usually with a whorled cut surface and no haemorrhagic or necrotic foci.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105094,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Considered different from its soft tissue counterpart, ganglioneuroma contains abundant bland Schwann cells (&gt;&nbsp;50% of tumour volume) arranged in sheets or fascicles with individually dispersed or clustered maturing and/or mature ganglion cells. Maturing ganglion cells vary in size and shape and may be multinucleated. Rarely, differentiating neuroblasts are present, but they are not nested and are without neuropil. Mature ganglion cells are covered by satellite cells. A lymphocytic infiltrate is common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105095,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105096,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105097,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a dominant Schwann cell component; maturing and/or mature ganglion cells; no mitoses.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> no nests of neuroblasts; no neuropil (naked neurites); no nodules of neuroblasts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105098,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The International Neuroblastoma Risk Group Staging System (INRGSS) is used for all neuroblastic tumours {19047290}, with clinical staging based on image-defined risk factors. Ganglioneuromas are locoregional and low-stage {19530234; 27465021; 29369484}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105099,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 453,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ganglioneuroma is categorized as having a favourable histology {10421272}. The prognosis is excellent for both subtypes, even with incomplete excision {11745303; 25501841; 27465021; 29369484}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:17:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]